  num:56, name:"Al-Wāqiʿah", ar:"الواقعة", en:"The Inevitable", verses:96, place:"Makkan",
  blurb:"THREE GROUPS — sorted on the DAY (v.7–56) and again at DEATH (v.88–94). FOUR \"have you seen?\": SEED, CROP, WATER, FIRE. Ends: ⟦حَقّ ٱلْيَقِينِ|ḥaqq al-yaqīn⟧ + the ⟦رُكُوعًا تَسْبِيح|rukūʿ tasbīḥ⟧.",
  special:["It sorts ALL of humanity into THREE groups — TWICE: once on the Day of Resurrection (v.7–56), and once at the moment of DEATH (v.88–94).","The three groups: - ⟦ٱلسَّـٰبِقُونَ|as-Sābiqūn⟧ — the FORERUNNERS, the ones brought NEAR (⟦ٱلْمُقَرَّبُونَ|al-muqarrabūn⟧) - ⟦أَصْحَـٰبَ ٱلْيَمِينِ|Aṣḥāb al-Yamīn⟧ / ⟦ٱلْمَيْمَنَةِ|al-Maymanah⟧ — the PEOPLE OF THE RIGHT (the saved) - ⟦أَصْحاب ٱلشِّمَالِ|Aṣḥāb ash-Shimāl⟧ / ⟦ٱلْمَشْـَٔمَةِ|al-Mashʾamah⟧ — the PEOPLE OF THE LEFT (the lost)","And the ending REPEATS the sorting at the DEATHBED: v.88–89 — if he is one of the ⟦مُقَرَّبُونَ|muqarrabūn⟧ → ⟦رَوْحٌ وَرَيْحَانٌ|rawḥ wa rayḥān⟧ (rest and fragrance). v.90–91 — if one of the people of the right → ⟦سَلَٰمٌ|salām⟧. v.92–94 — if one of the deniers → boiling water and Hellfire. The great sorting of the Day (opening) happens in miniature at every single death (ending).","In the middle: FOUR \"Have you seen…?\" questions (⟦أَفَرَءَيْتُم|a-fa-raʾaytum⟧) — the seed you emit, the crop you plant, the water you drink, the fire you kindle — \"did YOU create it — or did WE?\"","It closes with ⟦حَقّ ٱلْيَقِينِ|ḤAQQ AL-YAQĪN⟧ (v.95) — the TOP rung of the certainty ladder (⟦عِلْم|ʿilm⟧ → ʿayn → ⟦حَقُّ ٱلْيَقِينِ|ḥaqq al-yaqīn⟧), the same phrase as Ḥāqqah 69:51 — and ⟦فَسَبِّحْ بِٱسْمِ رَبِّكَ ٱلْعَظِيمِ|fa-sabbiḥ bismi rabbika'l-ʿaẓīm⟧ (v.74, 96) — the words of your ⟦رُكُوعًا|RUKŪʿ⟧.","Abū Bakr said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you've gone grey!\" He ﷺ replied: \"Hūd, ⟦ٱلْوَاقِعَةُ|al-Wāqiʿah⟧, ⟦ٱلْمُرْسَلَٰتِ|al-Mursalāt⟧, ⟦عَمَّ يَتَسَآءَلُونَ|ʿAmma yatasāʾalūn⟧ and Idha'sh-shamsu ⟦كُوِّرَتْ|kuwwirat⟧ turned me grey\" (Tirmidhī). (A popular report about reciting it nightly against poverty exists — its chain is weak by most scholars' assessment.)","--"],
  big:["The Event (v.1–6) — when it happens, no one will deny it; it lowers and raises; earth shaken, mountains crumbled to dust.","Three groups (v.7–10) — right, left, and the forerunners.","The Forerunners (v.11–26) — near to Allah, couches, cups, fruit, companions, peace.","The People of the Right (v.27–40) — thornless lote trees, extended shade, endless fruit.","The People of the Left (v.41–56) — scorching wind, boiling water, black smoke; the tree of Zaqqūm.","\"Have you seen…?\" (v.57–74) — the seed, the crop, the water, the fire.","The oath by the stars (v.75–82) — a noble Qurʾān, in a protected book, touched only by the purified.","The deathbed (v.83–96) — when the soul reaches the throat; the three groups at death; the truth of certainty."],
  traps:["لَجَعَلْنَاهُ حُطَامًا (v.65) vs جَعَلْنَاهُ أُجَاجًا (v.70) — WITH lām vs WITHOUT — a famous classical puzzle.","الضَّالُّونَ الْمُكَذِّبُونَ (v.51) vs الْمُكَذِّبِينَ الضَّالِّينَ (v.92) — order reversed.","فَلَوْلَا... فَلَوْلَا... تَرْجِعُونَهَا (v.83–87) — one suspended sentence — the verb of ⟦لَوْلَآ|lawlā⟧ arrives in v.87.","لَقَسَمٌ لَّوْ تَعْلَمُونَ عَظِيمٌ (v.76) — ⟦لَوْ تَعْلَمُونَ|law taʿlamūn⟧ wedged between noun and adjective.","تَصْلِيَةُ (ṣ-l-y, roast) ≠ صَلَاة (ṣ-l-w, prayer).","ثُلَّةٌ... وَقَلِيلٌ (v.13–14) vs ثُلَّةٌ... وَثُلَّةٌ (v.39–40) — one word changes everything.","فُرُشٍ (beds) ≠ فَرَاش (moths — 101:4).","الْآخِرِينَ (⟦آخِر|ākhir⟧, later) ≠ آخَرِينَ (⟦آخَر|ākhar⟧, others — 62:3).","إِنشَاء (construction) ≠ إِن شَاءَ اللَّهُ (if Allah wills).","فَظَلْتُمْ (v.65) — = ẓalaltum (one lām dropped); تَذَكَّرُونَ (v.62) = ⟦تَتَذَكَّرُونَ|tatadhakkarūn⟧ (one tāʾ dropped).","وَكُنتُمْ (v.7) — PAST for certain FUTURE.","إِلَّا قِيلًا سَلَامًا (v.26) — disconnected exception (munqaṭiʿ).","لَا يَمَسُّهُ (v.79) — NEGATION in form (debated as prohibition).","فَسَلَامٌ لَّكَ (v.91) — sudden 2nd person (iltifāt).","بِاسْمِ (v.74, 96) — alif PRESENT in the rasm (dropped only in the basmalah).","فِي مَا (v.61) · جَنَّتُ (v.89) — written separately / open tāʾ (rasm).","إِنَّ هَٰذَا لَهُوَ (v.95) — TRIPLE emphasis.","ثَلَاثَةً (v.7) — reverse gender.","وَحُورٌ عِينٌ (v.22) — variant ⟦حُورٍ عِينٍ|ḥūrin ʿīnin⟧.","فَرَوْحٌ (v.89) — variant fa-rūḥun.","مِنْهَا... عَلَيْهِ (v.53–54) — feminine then masculine pronoun (the tree / what was eaten).","بِمَوَاقِعِ (v.75) — variant bi-mawqiʿi."],
